# IWSDK's toolchain assumes npm's flat node_modules.
#
# `@iwsdk/vite-plugin-dev` pre-bundles its own transitive dependencies and then
# resolves their imports from the *application's* directory rather than from the
# package that declares them. Under npm that works by accident; under pnpm's
# strict layout Vite fails with "Failed to resolve import" for
# @zappar/msdf-generator, @babylonjs/havok and friends, and `pnpm demo` dies
# before the world starts.
#
# Hoisting the specific offenders is the narrow fix. `shamefully-hoist=true`
# would also work and is what most projects reach for, but it would expose every
# transitive dependency to `packages/client` too — and that package is the
# published artefact, so its inability to reach an undeclared dependency is a
# property worth keeping.
public-hoist-pattern[]=@babylonjs/*
public-hoist-pattern[]=@zappar/*
public-hoist-pattern[]=@drawcall/*
public-hoist-pattern[]=@iwsdk/scene-composition
public-hoist-pattern[]=three-viewport-gizmo
